-- title:
--   Nilpotent coordinates on X[p] for a pure edge branch
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a Noetherian commutative ring $R$ of characteristic $p$, together with a ring homomorphism $j\colon W(\mathbb F_{p^2})\to R$ (here $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ is realised as the Witt vectors of `GaloisField p 2`) and an element $\xi\in R$. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $R$, that is, a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $R$ equipped with an action $a\mapsto \mathrm{act}(a)$ of $W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ by endomorphism power series of $F$ (unital, multiplicative for composition, additive for $F$) and a further endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}(a)=\mathrm{act}(\sigma a)\circ\varpi$ for the Frobenius $\sigma$. Let $\gamma_0,\gamma_1$ be elements of the Cartier module of $F$ forming a homogeneous $V$-basis with respect to $j$: $\gamma_i$ lies in the $i$-th graded piece, i.e. the Teichmüller part of the action scales $\gamma_i$ by $j(\omega(c))^{p^i}$ for every $c\in\mathbb F_{p^2}$, and the matrix of tangent coefficients $(\mathrm{tangent}(\gamma_i)_k)$ has unit determinant. Assume the structure constants of $\gamma$ for $\varpi$ are the edge constants with parameters $(\xi,0)$: for each $i$ and each $N$ one has $\varpi_*\gamma_i=\sum_{m<N}V^m\bigl(a_{m,i}\gamma_{(m+i+1)\bmod 2}\bigr)+V^N h$ for some Cartier module element $h$, where $a_{m,0}$ is given by the branch constants of $0$ and $a_{m,1}$ by those of $\xi$, the branch constants of $x$ being $x^p-x$ at $m=0$, $1$ at $m=1$, the $(m/2)$-th Witt digit of $x$ raised to $p^{m/2}$ for even $m\ge 2$, and $0$ for odd $m\ge 3$. The conclusion is that there exists $N\in\mathbb N$ such that for both $i\in\{0,1\}$ the power $X_i^N$ lies in the ideal of $R[[X_0,X_1]]$ generated by the two component series of $\mathrm{act}(p)$, the power series giving multiplication by $p$ on $X$.
--
--   The assertion is that the kernel of multiplication by $p$ on such a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module is infinitesimal of finite order, so that the coordinate functions are nilpotent modulo the ideal of $[p]$; over a Noetherian base this is what makes the kernel algebra finite and allows it to be compared after base change. This case $\eta=0$ of the edge family is the pure-branch input to the corresponding statement for general edge constants $(\xi,\eta)$ with $\xi\eta=0$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_exists_X_pow_mem_span_act_of_hasStructureConstants_edgeConstants_zero.lean

